coder › Done. Implemented `parseIni` in `src/ini.ts` and added the 8 tests to `src/ini.test.ts` (existing section test kept), committed as `e3a5f19` on `work/main`.

**Key behavior notes:**
- Section headers create their section eagerly (`'[a]'` alone → `{ a: {} }`); the `''` section is created lazily only when a pre-header key is assigned, so no stray `''` key appears when a real header exists.
- Quoted values: only stripped when the trimmed value has length ≥ 2 and both starts and ends with `"`; the interior is kept verbatim (spaces and `;` preserved). No inline-comment stripping.
- First `=` splits key/value; everything trimmed; syntax errors throw `SyntaxError` with the 1-based line number (counting comments/blanks since every split line is iterated).

**Tests added:** pre-section keys under `''`, whitespace trimming, comments/blank lines, quoted value verbatim, first-`=` split (`k=b=c`), override + separate sections, and error line numbers (`/line 3/`, `/line 1/`).

